[\p{L}--[a-z]]+|[\q{abc|d}0-9]{2,}?\p{S…  one of 2 alternatives
├─ [\p{L}--[a-z]]+                        characters in the first set but not in the others, 1 or more (greedy)
│  ├─ \p{L}                               any of: a letter (Unicode L)
│  └─ [a-z]                               any of: a-z
└─ [\q{abc|d}0-9]{2,}?\p{Script=Greek}    alternative 2
   ├─ [\q{abc|d}0-9]{2,}?                 any of: string "abc" or "d", 0-9, 2 or more (lazy)
   └─ \p{Script=Greek}                    a character with Unicode property "Script=Greek"
